{% set local_problem %}
<p>Arab's hillside location and abundant tree coverage create a perfect storm for clogged gutters. Oak leaves pile up in fall. Pine needles accumulate year-round. And when gutters clog on sloped terrain, the consequences are worse than on flat land — overflow water gains velocity as it runs downhill toward your foundation (roughly 1.5x faster on a 10% grade).</p>

<p>Many Arab homeowners put off gutter cleaning because it's dangerous, time-consuming, and unpleasant. Climbing extension ladders on uneven hillside terrain is risky even for experienced people. Reaching all sections of gutters on a multi-level hillside home often requires specialized equipment most homeowners don't have.</p>

<p>The cost of neglecting gutters far exceeds the cost of cleaning them. Foundation repairs in the area average $10,000-30,000. Fascia board replacement runs $1,000-3,000. A couple of professional cleanings per year is a bargain compared to those alternatives.</p>

<p><strong>The math:</strong> Annual cleaning (twice yearly) costs $250-400 total. Skipping cleanings until problems develop costs $10,000+ in foundation or fascia repairs. We've seen this pattern repeatedly — homeowners skip a few cleanings, overflow damages foundation, and now they're facing five-figure repair bills. Don't learn this lesson the expensive way.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our cleaning service is thorough, not rushed.</p>

<p><strong>Step 1: Hand removal.</strong> We pull all debris from gutter troughs by hand — leaves, pine needles, roof grit, decomposed organic matter. We don't blow it onto your lawn or push it toward downspouts (a common shortcut that moves the problem rather than solving it). We bag everything and haul it away.</p>

<p><strong>Step 2: Downspout flush.</strong> Every downspout gets flushed with water until it runs clear. This is critical and the #1 thing homeowners miss during DIY cleaning. Debris backs up in the downspout, water can't exit, and gutters overflow even though they look clean from above. If someone cleans your gutters and doesn't flush downspouts, you're not getting complete service.</p>

<p><strong>Step 3: Inspection.</strong> While we're up there, we check for: loose or missing hangers, seam separations, small leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage. We press on fascia to check for soft spots — visual inspection alone misses hidden rot. Paint can look fine while wood underneath has gone soft. We document problems and let you know — no scare tactics, just honest assessment.</p>

<p><strong>Step 4: Cleanup.</strong> When we leave, your property looks the same or better. No debris on the lawn, no mess in the landscaping.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>Our crews are trained, insured, and equipped to safely clean gutters on any <a href="/recent-projects/">Arab home</a> — including hillside properties with challenging access. We show up when we say we will, do thorough work, and treat your property with respect.</p>

<p>We're just 30 minutes away in Huntsville, so we serve Arab homeowners efficiently. Many of our customers switch from cleaning to gutter guards after experiencing our service — we'll help you determine which approach makes more sense for your situation and budget.</p>

<p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Schedule cleaning for late November (after leaves drop) and late April (after spring pollen/seeds). If you have heavy pine coverage, add one in August. Three cleanings a year keeps everything flowing. Or consider gutter guards if you're tired of the ongoing expense — they typically pay for themselves within 2-3 years in Arab's debris-heavy environment.</p>

